	Option Say "Busy seasons are rough! Is it the good kind of busy or the 'too much going on' variety?"

-- === SEASONAL & HOLIDAY TOPICS ===
-- Time-based conversation starters that are naturally relevant

Recognizer "spring"
	Remember "User mentioned spring"
	Option Say "Spring energy is so refreshing! Are you feeling the renewal vibes or still shaking off winter?"
	Option Say "Spring brings so many possibilities! Any seasonal activities or changes you're looking forward to?"

Recognizer "summer"
	Remember "User mentioned summer"
	Option Say "Summer has such a unique feeling! Are you soaking up the season or counting down to cooler weather?"
	Option Say "Summer activities are the best! Beach days, barbecues, outdoor adventures - what's calling to you?"

Recognizer "fall"
	Remember "User mentioned fall/autumn"
	Option Say "Fall is such a cozy season! Are you embracing the autumn vibes or sad to see summer go?"
	Option Say "Autumn has its own magic! Pumpkin everything, changing leaves, crisp air - what do you love about this season?"

Recognizer "winter"
	Remember "User mentioned winter"
	Option Say "Winter can be beautiful or brutal depending on where you are! How do you make the most of the cold months?"
	Option Say "Winter vibes are so specific! Cozy indoor time or outdoor snow activities - where do you find your joy?"

Recognizer "holiday"
	Remember "User mentioned holidays"
	Option Say "Holidays bring such a mix of emotions! Any traditions you love or stress you're trying to avoid?"
	Option Say "Holiday seasons can be wonderful and overwhelming at the same time! How do you navigate all the festivities?"

-- === CONVERSATION STARTERS ===
-- Direct small talk initiation patterns

Recognizer "what's new"
	Remember "User asked what's new"
	Option Say "That's the perfect question! Life's been a mix of routine and surprises. What's new in your world?"
	Option Say "I love that question because it's so open-ended! What's been happening lately that's worth sharing?"

Recognizer "how's life"
	Remember "User asked how life is"
	Option Say "Life's been good! Full of the usual ups and downs. How has life been treating you recently?"
	Option Say "Life keeps moving! Some days are better than others. What's your life looking like these days?"

Recognizer "anything interesting"
	Remember "User asked about interesting things"
	Option Say "Interesting is such a great way to think about experiences! What's been catching your attention lately?"
	Option Say "Interest is everywhere if you look for it! What's sparked your curiosity or made you think recently?"

Recognizer "tell me something"
	Remember "User wants to hear something"
	Option Say "I love open-ended requests! What kind of something - funny, surprising, thoughtful, random?"
	Option Say "Something could be anything! Are you looking for a story, an observation, or just curious conversation?"

-- === OPINION-BASED SMALL TALK ===
-- Topics that invite personal perspectives

Recognizer "opinion"
	Remember "User wants opinions"
	Option Say "Opinions make conversations interesting! What topic has you thinking or wanting different perspectives?"
	Option Say "Everyone has opinions! What's something you've been pondering or debating in your head?"

Recognizer "prefer"
	Remember "User asking about preferences"
	Option Say "Preferences reveal so much about people! What choice or decision has you weighing options?"
	Option Say "Personal preferences are fascinating! Are you trying to figure out your own opinion or curious about others?"

Recognizer "favorite"
	Remember "User asking about favorites"
	Option Say "Favorites are hard to choose sometimes! What category are you curious about - there are so many possibilities?"
	Option Say "Favorite things say a lot about us! What's got you thinking about top choices or preferences?"

-- === LIGHTHEARTED & FUN TOPICS ===
-- Playful conversation starters that work across personalities

Recognizer "random"
	Remember "User wants random conversation"
	Option Say "Random conversations can be the most fun! What kind of randomness are you in the mood for?"
	Option Say "I love random topics! They can lead anywhere. What's bouncing around in your head?"

Recognizer "weird"
	Remember "User mentioned weird things"
	Option Say "Weird can be wonderful! The world is full of delightfully strange things. What weirdness have you encountered?"
	Option Say "Weird observations make the best conversations! What's caught your attention for its oddity?"

Recognizer "funny"
	Remember "User wants funny topics"
	Option Say "Funny moments make everything better! Any recent laughs or amusing observations to share?"
	Option Say "Humor is so subjective and wonderful! What's been making you smile or laugh lately?"

Recognizer "interesting fact"
	Remember "User wants interesting facts"
	Option Say "Interesting facts are conversation gold! Any particular topic area you're curious about?"
	Option Say "Facts can be so surprising! What kind of knowledge has been catching your attention?"
